---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Colophon, Aditya Rathi" description="How adityarathi.com is built: type, drawings, and hosting.">
  <article class="measure colophon">
    <h1>Colophon</h1>
    <p>
      Text is set in <a href="https://github.com/huertatipografica/piazzolla">Piazzolla</a> by Huerta Tipográfica;
      numbers and code in <a href="https://github.com/IBM/plex">IBM Plex Mono</a> by IBM. Both are released under the
      SIL Open Font License (<a href="/fonts/OFL-Piazzolla.txt">Piazzolla licence</a>, <a
        href="/fonts/OFL-IBM-Plex-Mono.txt">Plex licence</a>) and served from this site.
    </p>
    <p>
      The diagrams are drawn with <a href="https://roughjs.com/">Rough.js</a> when the site is built, so they arrive as
      plain SVG with no script. The site is built with <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a> and hosted on GitHub Pages.
    </p>
    <p>No cookies.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .colophon {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-m);
    padding-block: var(--space-xl);
  }
</style>
